WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:14.759
Mr. Smith: Please pull out your workbooks.

2
00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:17.685
Tina: Sorry, Danny.

3
00:00:17.686 --> 00:00:22.215
Dave: We’ll see you at recess, Danny.

4
00:00:22.216 --> 00:00:26.051
Danny: No more clay?

5
00:00:26.052 --> 00:00:27.744
Mr. Smith: Now, Danny . . .

6
00:00:27.745 --> 00:00:29.777
Danny: Yes, Mr. Smith?

7
00:00:29.778 --> 00:00:32.291
Mr. Smith: You can’t yell in class.

8
00:00:32.292 --> 00:00:35.585
Danny: But they were being mean to me!

9
00:00:35.586 --> 00:00:37.365
Mr. Smith: Danny . . .

10
00:00:37.366 --> 00:00:39.540
Danny: They’re bullies!

11
00:00:39.541 --> 00:00:42.225
Mr. Smith: You were the one making all the noise.

12
00:00:42.226 --> 00:00:45.178
Danny: I’m just an excited guy!

13
00:00:45.179 --> 00:00:48.387
Mr. Smith: Danny, please throw out your clay.

14
00:00:48.388 --> 00:00:50.644
Danny: I don’t want to.

15
00:00:50.645 --> 00:01:00.375
Mr. Smith: Please do it now.

16
00:01:00.376 --> 00:01:05.042
Mr. Smith: Thank you. Now, go sit in the corner until recess.

17
00:01:05.043 --> 00:01:08.633
Danny: Please! I promise to be quiet!

18
00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:12.461
Mr. Smith: No. You’ll sit there and think about what you’ve done.

19
00:01:12.462 --> 00:01:15.460
Danny: Do I have to?

20
00:01:15.461 --> 00:01:20.544
Mr. Smith: Yes, Danny. You do.

21
00:01:20.545 --> 00:01:23.587
Brad: I thought your models looked good, Danny.

22
00:01:23.588 --> 00:01:26.813
Danny: Thanks. They’re garbage now.

23
00:01:26.814 --> 00:01:29.452
Tina: You tried to stand up to those bullies.

24
00:01:29.453 --> 00:01:31.100
Good for you.

25
00:01:31.101 --> 00:01:37.186
Danny: But now I’m in trouble.

26
00:01:37.187 --> 00:01:39.336
Dave: Ha-ha!

27
00:01:39.337 --> 00:01:41.618
Chuck: Ha-ha!

28
00:01:41.619 --> 00:01:45.262
Danny: It’s not fair.

29
00:01:45.263 --> 00:01:48.267
Mr. Smith: Now, Danny, I want you to put your head on the desk.

30
00:01:48.268 --> 00:01:50.404
[n3@And think about what you did.

31
00:01:50.405 --> 00:01:53.512
Danny: I was making great art, but . . .

32
00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:55.804
Mr. Smith: What’s the lesson, Danny?

33
00:01:55.805 --> 00:01:57.395
Danny: I don’t know.

34
00:01:57.396 --> 00:02:00.398
Mr. Smith: You shouldn’t get so excited in the future.

35
00:02:00.399 --> 00:02:03.080
Danny: I’ve got a great imagination!

36
00:02:03.081 --> 00:02:06.868
I can’t help it!

37
00:02:06.869 --> 00:02:11.024
Mr. Smith: Okay, class. Turn to page six in your books.

38
00:02:11.025 --> 00:02:15.205
Chuck: Hey, Danny. I’ll save that little doll you made.

39
00:02:15.206 --> 00:02:17.297
Danny: Leave me alone.

40
00:02:17.298 --> 00:02:22.953
Chuck: Then you can have it forever.

41
00:02:22.954 --> 00:02:28.670
Danny: Dumb people are always getting me into trouble . . .

42
00:02:28.671 --> 00:02:41.488
Danny: I just wanted to play with my clay. That’s all.

43
00:02:41.489 --> 00:02:43.615
Danny: Who’s that?
